WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.572
Often one summary measure is not enough.

00:00:02.572 --> 00:00:08.822
We may want to know the number of orders, total revenue, and average order value for each channel.

00:00:08.822 --> 00:00:13.717
The agg method lets us calculate several measures in one grouped analysis.

00:00:13.717 --> 00:00:18.567
In this example, we group by channel and use named aggregation.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.137
Orders counts the number of records.

00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:25.512
Revenue sums the amount. Average order calculates the mean.

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:27.852
Click Run and look at the result.

00:00:27.852 --> 00:00:33.947
Named aggregation is especially useful because the output columns already have meaningful names.

00:00:33.947 --> 00:00:40.447
This is much easier to use in a report or dashboard than columns with confusing multi-level labels.

00:00:40.447 --> 00:00:41.927
Also notice as_index equals false.

00:00:41.927 --> 00:00:47.552
This keeps channel as a regular column rather than moving it into the index.

00:00:47.552 --> 00:00:54.627
When building summaries, think about the measures that answer the question.

00:00:54.627 --> 00:00:57.472
More metrics are not automatically better.

00:00:57.472 --> 00:01:01.295
Choose metrics that help someone understand the behavior of each group.
